# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
# Static export has no middleware, so locale entry and legacy-URL preservation
# are handled here at the edge instead.

# The bare root is deliberately absent here. `/` is served by a generated
# index.html that picks the locale from the reader's stored choice, then their
# browser's languages (scripts/write-root-router.mjs). An edge redirect would
# fire before that file is ever served, so the two cannot coexist — this is
# where the redirect used to be.

# Legacy SPA URLs. The old site served every language from these two paths and
# advertised itself as Korean, so equity is consolidated onto /ko/ and the
# preference handler forwards visitors of other languages.
/list        /ko/digimon/    301
/list/       /ko/digimon/    301

# Naver's site verification, served at the exact URL it asks for.
#
# Pages strips .html and 301s /foo.html to /foo, so the file Naver uploads is
# reachable at every address except the one Naver requests. A verifier that
# does not follow redirects simply fails. The 200 here is a rewrite rather than
# a redirect: same asset, no hop.
/navereb19e1bff7893892952288337f312e92.html  /navereb19e1bff7893892952288337f312e92  200
